      "id": "GENUS_ELEPHAS",
      "name": "Elephas",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Asian elephants — smaller than their African relatives with more domed foreheads, smaller ears, and a single 'finger' on the trunk tip (African elephants have two). Asian elephants have lived alongside humans for thousands of years and have been domesticated for use in forestry, transport, religious ceremonies, and warfare. The relationship is not truly domesticated — Asian elephants in captivity are tamed wild animals, not a domestic breed. Wild Asian elephants are endangered; their forest habitat across southern and southeast Asia is fragmented by agriculture, and they come into increasing conflict with human settlements as ranges contract.",
      "lineage": "Asian Elephants",
